## Modified `onDiscordMessage()` (~line 208-318)

Replace the guild message filtering logic (lines 218-222). Keep everything else (self-ignore, bot-ignore, handler check, content stripping, SubstrateMessage construction, lock/steer/pending pattern) unchanged.

New routing decision:
```
1. Ignore self, bots, no handler (unchanged)
2. DM → always process (unchanged)
3. Guild messages — check in order:
   a. !i prefix → return (ignore even during listening)
   b. @mentioned → process, open listening window
   c. content matches triggerWords OR characterName (case-insensitive) → process, open listening window
   d. user is in active listening window for this channel → process, extend window
   e. none of the above → return
```

Implementation sketch for the filtering section:
```ts
const isDM = !msg.guild;
const channelId = msg.channelId;
const userId = msg.author.id;

if (!isDM) {
  // !i prefix → always ignore
  if (msg.content.trimStart().startsWith('!i')) return;

  const isMentioned = runtimeBotId ? msg.mentions.has(runtimeBotId) : false;
  const isTriggered = this.matchesTriggerWord(msg.content);
  const listenKey = `${channelId}:${userId}`;
  const isListening = this.isInListeningWindow(listenKey);

  if (!isMentioned && !isTriggered && !isListening) return;

  // Open/extend listening window on any trigger
  this.openListeningWindow(listenKey);

  if (isTriggered && !isMentioned) log.debug('Trigger word matched', { channelId, trigger: true });
  if (isListening && !isTriggered && !isMentioned) log.debug('Active listening window', { channelId, userId });
}
```

**Important**: The `security.requiresMentionForChannelMessages` field (line 99) should now be set to `true` unconditionally (we have trigger words as the alternative to mentions, not `respondAll`).

## New private methods

### `matchesTriggerWord(content: string): boolean`
```ts
private matchesTriggerWord(content: string): boolean {
  const lower = content.toLowerCase();
  // Character name is always an implicit trigger
  const charName = this.runtimeConfig.characterName;
  if (charName && lower.includes(charName.toLowerCase())) return true;
  // Check configured trigger words
  const words = this.runtimeConfig.discordTriggerWords;
  if (words?.some(w => lower.includes(w.toLowerCase()))) return true;
  return false;
}
```

### `isInListeningWindow(key: string): boolean`
```ts
private isInListeningWindow(key: string): boolean {
  const expiry = this.listeningWindows.get(key);
  if (!expiry) return false;
  if (Date.now() > expiry) {
    this.listeningWindows.delete(key);
    return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

### `openListeningWindow(key: string): void`
```ts
private openListeningWindow(key: string): void {
  const windowMs = this.runtimeConfig.discordTriggerListenWindowMs ?? 120_000;
  this.listeningWindows.set(key, Date.now() + windowMs);
  log.debug('Listening window opened/extended', { key, windowMs });
}
```

### `onReactionAdd(reaction, user): Promise<void>`

```ts
private async onReactionAdd(
  reaction: MessageReaction | PartialMessageReaction,
  user: User | PartialUser,
): Promise<void> {
  // Ignore self and bots
  const botId = this.client.user?.id ?? this.runtimeConfig.discordBotId;
  if (user.id === botId) return;
  if (user.bot) return;

  const emojiName = reaction.emoji.name ?? '';

  // ❌ on bot's own message → delete it
  if (emojiName === '❌') {
    const fullReaction = reaction.partial ? await reaction.fetch() : reaction;
    const msg = fullReaction.message.partial ? await fullReaction.message.fetch() : fullReaction.message;
    if (msg.author.id === botId) {
      log.info('Delete reaction on bot message', { messageId: msg.id, channelId: msg.channelId });
      await msg.delete().catch(err => log.warn('Failed to delete bot message', { error: String(err) }));
    }
    return;
  }

  if (!this.handler) return;

  // Check configured trigger reactions
  const triggerReactions = this.runtimeConfig.discordTriggerReactions ?? ['👆'];
  if (triggerReactions.length === 0) return;

  const emojiId = reaction.emoji.id ? `<:${emojiName}:${reaction.emoji.id}>` : emojiName;
  const isMatch = triggerReactions.some(t => t === emojiName || t === emojiId);
  if (!isMatch) return;

  // Fetch partial data
  const fullReaction = reaction.partial ? await reaction.fetch() : reaction;
  const msg = fullReaction.message.partial ? await fullReaction.message.fetch() : fullReaction.message;

  // Don't respond to bot's own messages
  if (msg.author.id === botId || msg.author.bot) return;

  const channelId = msg.channelId;
  const content = msg.content?.trim() || '(empty message)';

  log.debug('Reaction trigger', { emoji: emojiName, channelId, messageId: msg.id });

  // Open listening windows for message author + reactor
  this.openListeningWindow(`${channelId}:${msg.author.id}`);
  if (user.id !== msg.author.id) {
    this.openListeningWindow(`${channelId}:${user.id}`);
  }

  // Remove the trigger reaction to acknowledge
  fullReaction.remove().catch(() => undefined);

  // Build SubstrateMessage and process through existing lock/handler path
  // Use the processMessage() extracted helper (see below)
  await this.processMessage(msg as Message, channelId, {
    id: msg.id,
    channelId,
    channelType: 'discord',
    isDirectMessage: false,
    authorId: msg.author.id,
    authorName: msg.author.displayName ?? msg.author.username,
    content,
    timestamp: msg.createdAt,
  }, true);  // replyToOriginal = true for reaction triggers
}
```

## Extract `processMessage()` helper

Refactor the lock-acquire → handler → send-response → lock-release logic from `onDiscordMessage()` into a shared `processMessage()` method. Both `onDiscordMessage()` and `onReactionAdd()` call it.

```ts
private async processMessage(
  msg: Message,
  channelId: string,
  substrateMsg: SubstrateMessage,
  replyToOriginal: boolean,
): Promise<void> {
  // ... existing lock/steer/pending pattern (unchanged) ...

  try {
    await this.eventBus.emit('message.received', { message: substrateMsg });
    const response = await this.handler(substrateMsg);
    const hasText = response.content.trim().length > 0;
    if (hasText) {
      if (replyToOriginal) {
        const chunks = splitMessage(response.content.trim());
        await msg.reply(chunks[0]);
        for (let i = 1; i < chunks.length; i++) {
          await (msg.channel as TextChannel).send(chunks[i]);
        }
      } else {
        await this.outbound.sendText({ channelId }, response.content);
      }
      await this.eventBus.emit('message.sent', { response });
    }
  } catch (error) { /* existing error handler */ }
  finally { /* existing cleanup + pendingByChannel replay (KEEP) */ }
}
```

**Key**: `replyToOriginal` is `true` ONLY for reaction triggers. Trigger words and listening window follow-ups use normal `sendText`.

## Cleanup on `stop()` (~line 180-186)

Add after existing cleanup:
```ts
this.listeningWindows.clear();
```

## New discord.js imports

Add to the import block (~line 1-8):
```ts
import {
  // existing...
  type MessageReaction,
  type PartialMessageReaction,
  type User,
  type PartialUser,
